{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Allure|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Evelynn
|skill        = W
|icon         = Allure.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Active:}} {{ci|Evelynn}} ''curses'' the target enemy, causing her next {{tip|basic attack}} or {{tip|ability}} against the target to ''expunge'' the ''curse'', {{tip|slow|slowing}} the target and refunding the {{sti|mana|{{as|mana cost}}}}.
|blurb2       = If the ''curse'' matures long enough, the ''expunge'' will increase the slow, {{tip|charm}} the target, and apply an additional effect based on the target type.
* {{tip|Champions}} have {{sti|magic penetration|{{as|reduced magic resist}}}} for a few seconds.
* {{tip|Monsters}} are dealt {{as|'''bonus''' magic damage}} and increased {{tip|charm}} duration.
|description  = {{sbc|Active:}} '''Evelynn''' marks the target enemy {{tip|champion}} or medium or large {{tip|monster}} with a curse for 5 seconds.
|description2 = '''Evelynn's''' next {{tip|basic attack}} or {{tip|ability}} hit against the target consumes the mark, {{tip|slow|slowing}} them by 45% for {{fd|0.75}} seconds and refunding ''Allure's'' {{as|{{sti|mana|mana cost}}}}. If the target was marked for at least {{fd|2.5}} seconds, the consumption is empowered.
|description3 =  {{sbc|Empowered Bonus:}} The target is {{tip|charm|charmed}} for a few seconds and the {{tip|slow}} duration is increased to the same period. Additional effects are also applied based on the target type:
* Against champions, inflicts a {{sti|magic penetration|{{as|magic resistance reduction}}}} for 4 seconds.
* Against monsters, the triggering effect deals {{as|'''bonus''' magic damage}} and the duration of the {{tip|charm}} is increased by {{fd|2.25}} seconds.
|leveling3    = {{st|Charm Duration|{{ap|1.25 to 2.25}} seconds}}
{{st|Magic Resistance Reduction|{{as|{{ap|35 to 45}}%|magic resistance}}}}
{{st|Bonus Magic Damage|{{ap|250 to 450}} {{as|(+ 60% AP)}}}}
{{st|Monster Charm Duration|{{ap|1.25+2.25 to 2.25+2.25}} seconds}}
|description4 = ''Casting Allure does not break {{ai|Demon Shade|Evelynn}} nor its fade into it.''
